  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nMid level flow will back more westerly through mid week with ridging\nat the surface and aloft offering dry conditions and above normal \ntemperatures through Wednesday. \n\nTemperatures moderate with highs Tuesday ranging from the lower 60s\nto the upper 60s. Cloud cover increases on Wednesday ahead of an \napproaching low pressure system but highs are still expected to be \nbetween 60 and 65. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\n\nA digging system upper level system will result in the development of\nlow pressure and the passage of a surface cold front late Wednesday \ninto Thursday. This system leads to an upper level low that develops\nover the Great Lakes late in the week and continues to influence our\nweather into the first part of the weekend. \n\nThere continues to be a decent amount of model spread regarding the \nstrength and path of the low. In general, rain develops Wednesday \nnight into Thursday morning. As the low progresses east of the area \non Thursday, much cooler temperatures will arrive along with a \nbrisk northerly flow. Any lingering wrap around precipitation could \nmix in with a few wet snow flakes by Friday.\n\nPrecipitation chances look to end Friday night. Cool conditions and \nbrisk northerly flow persists through the first part of the weekend, \nwith highs only in the 40s Friday and Saturday. Slight moderation\nwill occur with highs on Sunday in the upper 40s to around 50 and \n50 to 55 next Monday.",
